<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><description>Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/</link><lastBuildDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 17:31:51 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category><![CDATA[People & Profit]]></category><title>Food security under pressure from conflicts, extreme weather</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/people-profit/20260917-food-security-under-pressure-from-conflicts-extreme-weather</link><description>
Extreme weather and violent conflicts are threatening food production and trade across the globe. Experts are forecasting a super El Niño, which could further disrupt planting and harvests – and push millions more people into acute food insecurity. Meanwhile the ongoing wars with Iran and Ukraine are disrupting shipping and supply chains. 
 
Shawn Arita, Associate Research Professor at North Dakota State University, believes that transport problems outweigh supply concerns. "The food does exist, the availability does exist. The main issue currently speaking is that the movement is broken."  
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0fda0a8c-b2a2-11f1-9c1e-07ed91e97eb2/w:1024/p:16x9/ENMG-PEOPLE-AND-PROFIT-260917-2026-Ep-46-Copy-01.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0fda0a8c-b2a2-11f1-9c1e-07ed91e97eb2/w:1024/p:16x9/ENMG-PEOPLE-AND-PROFIT-260917-2026-Ep-46-Copy-01.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8c1817ac-b2a1-11f1-9235-df34d358e216</guid><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 16:21:07 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Kate MOODY</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Climate change: Glacier loss and dry rivers threaten water security</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260917-climate-change-glacier-loss-and-dry-rivers-threaten-water-security</link><description>
The world's rivers experienced one of their driest years in more than three decades in 2025, while glaciers continued to retreat and freshwater reserves kept declining, according to the World Meteorological Organization. The agency warns that climate change and growing water use are making the global water cycle more erratic, increasing the risk of both droughts and floods.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9b16c9aa-b2b1-11f1-a418-430f3874e448/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260917-171145-171339-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9b16c9aa-b2b1-11f1-a418-430f3874e448/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260917-171145-171339-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a0e4a4c4-b2b1-11f1-a274-1b2c56fb7208</guid><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 16:10:02 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Perspective</category><title>'Sanctions won’t prevent us from doing our job' says ICC Prosecutor Mame Mandiaye Niang</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20260917-sanctions-won-t-prevent-us-from-doing-our-job-says-icc-prosecutor-mame-mandiaye-niang</link><description>
In this edition of Perspective, the acting Prosecutor of the International Criminal Court tells FRANCE 24 that the court is needed now more than ever to ensure there is no gap for impunity. Mame Mandiaye Niang says the court’s job is to step in if domestic justice systems fail. The Senegalese judge is at the centre of a storm amid sanctions put on the court by the US after its issuing of arrest warrants for Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu and former Defence Minister Yoav Gallant over Israel’s actions in Gaza. He explained how the sanctions affect his daily life but says it won’t stop the court doing its job.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/332e1d38-b27b-11f1-8dd7-4daf57bffe27/w:1024/p:16x9/ANGL260917-0940-Live-CS0940.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/332e1d38-b27b-11f1-8dd7-4daf57bffe27/w:1024/p:16x9/ANGL260917-0940-Live-CS0940.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">42111864-b27b-11f1-8a60-a3ca3ffd93d4</guid><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 16:02:51 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Stuart NORVAL</dc:creator></item><item><category>arts24</category><title>Nicolas Winding Refn on nearly dying, reuniting with Ryan Gosling and why 'polarisation is success'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20260917-nicolas-winding-refn-on-nearly-dying-reuniting-with-ryan-gosling-and-why-polarisation-is-success</link><description>
Ten years after The Neon Demon, Nicolas Winding Refn is back with 'Her Private Hell', a neon-soaked fever dream starring Sophie Thatcher and Charles Melton. Speaking to FRANCE 24’s Eve Jackson at the Deauville American Film Festival, the Danish provocateur behind 'Drive' and 'Bronson' opens up about the near-death experience that changed his life, why he believes “polarisation is success” and his plans to make a third film with Ryan Gosling – 15 years after 'Drive'.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/29e52a74-b289-11f1-bacf-4daf57bffe27/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-2813641446aabcbf0782c73-63862335.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/29e52a74-b289-11f1-bacf-4daf57bffe27/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-2813641446aabcbf0782c73-63862335.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">95f44290-b289-11f1-8c59-9d7b52c60fdd</guid><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 15:38:33 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Eve JACKSON</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Gaza documentary 'NAZA' sparks political storm, threats against directors in Israel</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260917-gaza-documentary-naza-sparks-political-storm-in-israel</link><description>
The award-winning documentary "NAZA" featuring anonymous military sources speaking about Israel's mass killing of civilians in Gaza has sparked a political firestorm in Israel. The film's directors and their families have received a wave of threats, while Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu announced a plan for a bill aimed at revoking the citizenship of people who "defame IDF soldiers".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c69183f2-b2b8-11f1-a9f1-61f6f55d211c/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26258555934130.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c69183f2-b2b8-11f1-a9f1-61f6f55d211c/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26258555934130.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e73ee87c-b2ab-11f1-bad0-7d4ece9fee5a</guid><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 15:24:40 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c69183f2-b2b8-11f1-a9f1-61f6f55d211c/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26258555934130.jpg">© Ariel Schalit, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Spain: Images of floods after torrential rain</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260917-spain-images-of-floods-after-torrential-rain</link><description>
At least one person was killed after torrential rain lashed eastern Spain overnight Wednesday, submerging streets and flooding buildings and metro stations.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/317d9f02-b2aa-11f1-8aa4-430f3874e448/w:1024/p:16x9/Spain-floods-thumbnail.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/317d9f02-b2aa-11f1-8aa4-430f3874e448/w:1024/p:16x9/Spain-floods-thumbnail.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">bc5107b6-b2a7-11f1-bfac-557ac48fb40d</guid><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 15:23:17 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>English village holds symbolic vote to leave UK</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/english-village-holds-symbolic-vote-to-leave-uk</link><description>
A village in Oxfordshire has held a symbolic referendum to leave the United Kingdom in protest against government plans to house up to 1,200 asylum seekers at a nearby military base. While the vote has no legal force, it highlights wider tensions over the UK's asylum policy and migration debate.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ce9f6e32-b2a5-11f1-b76e-d7a11ace016d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260917-153343-153523-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ce9f6e32-b2a5-11f1-b76e-d7a11ace016d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260917-153343-153523-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d42c4c08-b2a5-11f1-a91e-5182ddc2f54d</guid><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 15:17:08 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Mbappé draws fire from right wing in France, Spain over Ceuta t-shirt controversy</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260917-real-madrid-s-mbapp%C3%A9-draws-criticism-from-far-right-over-ceuta-t-shirt-controversy</link><description>
Real Madrid's French forward Kylian Mbappé is facing mounting criticism by Spanish and French conservative and far-right politicians for partially obscuring a t-shirt supporting residents of Ceuta, Spain's territory bordering Morocco grappling with a migration crisis. Mbappé said he wore the t-shirt rolled up to show solidarity with "all the immigrants who have lost their lives".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2cdb4d4c-b281-11f1-a800-d7a11ace016d/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-16T175859Z-738929787-RC2XJNAL5KN5-RTRMADP-3-SOCCER-SPAIN-ELC-RMA.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2cdb4d4c-b281-11f1-a800-d7a11ace016d/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-16T175859Z-738929787-RC2XJNAL5KN5-RTRMADP-3-SOCCER-SPAIN-ELC-RMA.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f2260510-b2a9-11f1-8156-39eb0f836866</guid><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 15:10:39 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2cdb4d4c-b281-11f1-a800-d7a11ace016d/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-16T175859Z-738929787-RC2XJNAL5KN5-RTRMADP-3-SOCCER-SPAIN-ELC-RMA.jpg">© Omar Arnau Cerezo, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Amnesty accuses Iran of crimes against humanity</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/amnesty-accuses-iran-of-crimes-against-humanity</link><description>
Amnesty International has accused Iranian authorities of committing crimes against humanity during the 2022 Woman, Life, Freedom crackdown, saying more than 500 people, including 71 children, were killed and that the violence disproportionately targeted Kurdish and Baluchi communities. The rights group is urging the UN General Assembly to create an international justice mechanism, arguing that many of the officials it identified remain in positions of power.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b819a372-b2a4-11f1-b669-6db10b20ba37/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260917-152151-152343-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b819a372-b2a4-11f1-b669-6db10b20ba37/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260917-152151-152343-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">bd4d2396-b2a4-11f1-bcb2-6961acb57df3</guid><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 14:55:34 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Houthis claim Saudi F-15 kill as Yemen fighting escalates</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/houthis-claim-saudi-f-15-kill-as-yemen-fighting-escalates</link><description>
Yemen's Houthi rebels have released footage they say shows the wreckage of a Saudi F-15 fighter jet, which, if confirmed, would mark the first fighter jet they have shot down. The claim comes as fighting escalates in Yemen, with the Houthis expanding their control around the strategic Bab al-Mandab Strait and the UN urging both sides to return to negotiations.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4e0dde78-b2a2-11f1-98e8-991cccd3bb73/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260917-141009-141202-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4e0dde78-b2a2-11f1-98e8-991cccd3bb73/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260917-141009-141202-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1db0b8ba-b2a5-11f1-853c-6148f6ccb5da</guid><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 14:53:00 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Carney pushes Canada-EU ties beyond trade</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/carney-pushes-canada-eu-ties-beyond-trade</link><description>
Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney used his address to the European Parliament to signal that Ottawa wants to deepen its partnership with the EU beyond trade, expanding cooperation on energy, AI, space and payment sovereignty, while also seeking to join the Erasmus programme. FRANCE 24's Dave Keating explains how the push reflects Canada's broader strategy to build stronger alliances beyond the United States without seeking to join the EU's single market, even as questions remain over how those ambitions can be turned into concrete action.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fa6b4696-b28a-11f1-a748-4daf57bffe27/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-17T111429Z-20141978-RC2ZKNAG3C67-RTRMADP-3-EU-CANADA.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fa6b4696-b28a-11f1-a748-4daf57bffe27/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-17T111429Z-20141978-RC2ZKNAG3C67-RTRMADP-3-EU-CANADA.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">31e55368-b2a5-11f1-a3c2-fd76b89f47a3</guid><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 14:52:51 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'We must 'force' social media to redesign harmful algorithms, platforms that fuel addictive behavior</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/we-must-force-social-media-to-regulate-algorithms-and-harmful-platforms-designed-to-push-content</link><description>
Charles Pellegrin is pleased to welcome Hannah Storey, Head of Children and Young People’s Digital Rights at Amnesty International. Digital spaces can provide even young people with community, self-expression, education and opportunities for activism. The deeper problem, she warns, lies in the architecture of the platforms themselves: the algorithms, infinite scrolling and other engagement mechanisms that can repeatedly amplify harmful material, stir up negative emotions and incite troubling behaviours - all to bolster a business model built around attention, emotions, addition, data and advertising. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1630abb2-b2a6-11f1-9dd6-d7a11ace016d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260917-081043-081916-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1630abb2-b2a6-11f1-9dd6-d7a11ace016d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260917-081043-081916-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1b6511f4-b2a6-11f1-8989-07158fcc7245</guid><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 14:52:00 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Brazil election: Lula vows to stand up to Trump</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/brazil-election-lula-vows-to-stand-up-to-trump</link><description>
Brazilian President Lula says he will confront President Donald Trump at the UN in New York, accusing him of interfering in Brazil's election as tensions between Washington and Brasília deepen. The dispute comes after US tariffs on Brazilian goods and Trump's support for Lula's rival, Flavio Bolsonaro, the son of former president Jair Bolsonaro.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/345cc18c-8e95-11f1-b4f7-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C3TD7FG.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/345cc18c-8e95-11f1-b4f7-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C3TD7FG.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">24a7f6b0-b2a5-11f1-afaa-2fac250903fa</guid><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 14:47:39 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Lebanon on Paris talks : 'the general sentiment here is very little hope'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/lebanon-on-paris-talks-the-general-sentiment-here-is-very-little-hope</link><description>
Lebanese President Joseph Aoun is in Paris for talks with Emmanuel Macron, but on the ground many Lebanese say they have little hope after months of war with Israel, the continued occupation of parts of southern Lebanon and uncertainty over regional tensions. FRANCE 24's Renée David reports from Beirut on hopes that Aoun and Macron can rally international backing and secure a framework agreement to help stabilise the country.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8d9744b0-b2a4-11f1-815e-4daf57bffe27/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260917-141204-141501-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8d9744b0-b2a4-11f1-815e-4daf57bffe27/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260917-141204-141501-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">93091b44-b2a4-11f1-a558-7f456347e22f</guid><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 14:46:07 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Entre Nous</category><title>From Then to Now: European Heritage Days and saving France's 'patrimoine'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/entre-nous/20260917-from-then-to-now-european-heritage-days-and-saving-france-s-patrimoine</link><description>
Whether it’s visiting a national monument, going behind-the-scenes at a television station or walking around a neighbour’s castle, millions participate every year in The European Heritage Days. We dive into how they got their start, why they're needed now more than ever, and how there's a new deal – the Patrimoine Pass – to support France's monuments. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/12c01f7c-b2a0-11f1-b523-991cccd3bb73/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-11237339186aabf260047b59-39270028.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/12c01f7c-b2a0-11f1-b523-991cccd3bb73/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-11237339186aabf260047b59-39270028.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">750db78c-b2a2-11f1-b7b7-39560504e8d0</guid><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 14:30:31 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Solange MOUGIN</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US interest rate hike sparks Trump backlash</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/us-interest-rate-hike-sparks-trump-backlash</link><description>
The US Federal Reserve has raised interest rates for the first time since 2023, citing stubborn inflation despite pressure from President Donald Trump to cut borrowing costs. The decision prompted an immediate rebuke from Trump, while Fed Chair Kevin Warsh defended the central bank's independence and warned that inflation remains the priority.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/46cfe290-b29e-11f1-bac2-4daf57bffe27/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260917-140754-140925-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/46cfe290-b29e-11f1-bac2-4daf57bffe27/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260917-140754-140925-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4cccbb28-b29e-11f1-bbf0-0bf69855a15f</guid><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 14:21:23 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Entre Nous</category><title>Paris, the ultimate film set</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/entre-nous/20260917-paris-the-ultimate-film-set</link><description>
Paris has been a muse for filmmakers for over a century. The French capital has inspired countless scenes on the big screen. A new book brings them all together. Ruby Boukabou, author of 'The Movie Lovers' Guide to Paris', joins us to talk through her movie-themed walking tours in some of the city's most cinematic neighbourhoods.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2596e4d8-b268-11f1-bb67-0dbbad64a63b/w:1024/p:16x9/WB237104-O-01-20260917-01.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2596e4d8-b268-11f1-bb67-0dbbad64a63b/w:1024/p:16x9/WB237104-O-01-20260917-01.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">79db0ea6-b269-11f1-9f32-ed32a03b3854</guid><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 13:38:38 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Amanda ALEXANDER</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>DR Congo says Ebola outbreak has passed its peak</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/dr-congo-says-ebola-outbreak-has-passed-its-peak</link><description>
More than 3,510 people have died from Ebola in eastern DR Congo since the outbreak was declared four months ago, with Ituri accounting for 78% of confirmed cases. Congolese authorities say the epidemic has now passed its peak, pointing to signs that the outbreak is beginning to slow.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/251f5dca-b298-11f1-9d17-991cccd3bb73/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260916-214314-214535-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/251f5dca-b298-11f1-9d17-991cccd3bb73/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260916-214314-214535-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2b0aa3a2-b298-11f1-98e1-35a318fe9dfa</guid><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 13:36:09 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Zimbabwe farmers brace for El Niño by saving water</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260917-zimbabwe-farmers-brace-for-el-ni%C3%B1o-by-saving-water</link><description>
Some communities in Zimbabwe are adopting water-saving techniques such as aquaponics and rainwater harvesting to protect crops as the country braces for El Niño-driven drought. Sharon Mazingaizo has this report.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1ec4d298-b298-11f1-98d9-4daf57bffe27/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260916-215122-215323-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1ec4d298-b298-11f1-98d9-4daf57bffe27/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260916-215122-215323-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2540b0b0-b298-11f1-8f02-112304533c3c</guid><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 13:33:33 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Tigray: 20,000 university students relocated by conflict</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tigray-20-000-university-students-relocated-by-conflict</link><description>
Ethiopia's Education Ministry says around 20,000 university students in Tigray will be temporarily relocated to other public campuses after accusing the TPLF of using universities as military bases. The move comes as fighting and drone strikes continue in the northern region, with many students saying the trauma of the 2020-2022 Tigray war is still fresh. Our correspondent Tom Canetti reports from Addis Ababa.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/309e90ee-b298-11f1-9648-991cccd3bb73/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260916-214840-215041-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/309e90ee-b298-11f1-9648-991cccd3bb73/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260916-214840-215041-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3b0dfb50-b298-11f1-9fbe-35a318fe9dfa</guid><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 13:30:51 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Senegal farmers turn to fish and rice farming</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/senegal-farmers-turn-to-fish-and-rice-farming</link><description>
Some farmers in northern Senegal are combining fish farming with rice cultivation, using an age-old technique that helps fertilise fields, reduce pests and diversify incomes. The climate-smart approach is gaining renewed attention as communities adapt to growing environmental pressures.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3546f17c-b298-11f1-80da-d7a11ace016d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260916-215341-215523-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3546f17c-b298-11f1-80da-d7a11ace016d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260916-215341-215523-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3efd3a8c-b298-11f1-8b5b-df24e8f07957</guid><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 13:28:56 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Lebanon: UNIFIL withdrawal at the heart of Paris talks</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/lebanon-unifil-withdrawal-at-the-heart-of-paris-talks</link><description>
Emmanuel Macron welcomes Lebanese President Joseph Aoun and Jordan's King Abdullah II to Paris today for talks on Lebanon's security and international support for the Lebanese army. The meeting comes as France pushes to prevent a security vacuum ahead of UNIFIL's planned withdrawal at the end of 2026, with Israeli strikes continuing in southern Lebanon and concerns growing over who will secure the border. FRANCE 24's Luke Shrago has the latest.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d493f712-b297-11f1-8ba9-07ed91e97eb2/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260917-130744-131215-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d493f712-b297-11f1-8ba9-07ed91e97eb2/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260917-130744-131215-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d9f5b718-b297-11f1-92f4-d3e82812b02d</guid><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 13:23:41 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Sweden: Andersson's centre left claims narrow win</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/sweden-andersson-s-centre-left-claims-narrow-win</link><description>
Sweden's centre-left opposition, led by Magdalena Andersson, is set to defeat the incumbent right-wing bloc by one seat after nearly all votes were counted in Sunday's election. The narrow result means coalition talks are likely to be challenging, with parliament due to begin the government formation process on September 28.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a5531ffa-b297-11f1-af34-d7a11ace016d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260917-131830-131930-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a5531ffa-b297-11f1-af34-d7a11ace016d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260917-131830-131930-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">aab972c8-b297-11f1-b100-95518b0bca84</guid><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 13:22:19 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>Erdogan to sidestep Turkey’s constitutional term limits in early 2028 vote, adviser says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260917-turkey-s-erdogan-to-run-in-early-2028-vote-sidestepping-constitutional-term-limit</link><description>
Turkish President Recep Tayyip Erdogan intends to run in an early election in 2028 in order to circumvent the constitutional term limits he would face if he serves out his full current term, a top adviser said Thursday. Under Turkey's constitution, parliament can trigger early elections given the support of 360 lawmakers, meaning the ruling AKP and its nationalist ally MHP will need support of at least 34 more lawmakers. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4d859114-b2a5-11f1-91f1-a1d0582895b1/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26244537919329.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4d859114-b2a5-11f1-91f1-a1d0582895b1/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26244537919329.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">61db83a0-b299-11f1-ac71-d3d2a32cd2e1</guid><pubDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 13:12:06 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4d859114-b2a5-11f1-91f1-a1d0582895b1/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26244537919329.jpg">© Vyacheslav Prokofyev, Sputnik, Kremlin Pool Photo via AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item></channel></rss>
